	"nodes":[
		{"id":"490eb80b5a9f0b94","type":"text","text":"I am a curious and extrovert person who is fascinated by complex problems. I am always eager to broaden my knowledge and listen to others. I’m a team player, in the work environment as well as on the basketball court. Focused on improving rather than settling down. Loving kindness within its limitations.","x":240,"y":-774,"width":520,"height":214},
		{"id":"3792d521b037b9ff","type":"text","text":"## Scholarships and awards\n- 2025, [Poster winner at ChemAI 2025](https://www.linkedin.com/posts/giulio-benedini-60a7a4192_chemai-ugcPost-7399424216883781633-jBI0/)\n- 2017, from Politecnico di Milano, “best freshman award”\n- 2017-2021, from Politecnico di Milano, “students with high merits”, four consecutive years\n- 2020, from GSK S.p.A., “high merit scholarship”\n","x":240,"y":-520,"width":520,"height":446},
		{"id":"998872f15bfe1417","type":"text","text":"\n## Extra activities\n- 2025-10, **seminar** (90 min): \"From universal to specialised ML potentials for infrared spectra\", EuSpecLab Training School, Rennes (France)\n- 2025-05, **Co-organiser** of [Belgian-German WE-Heraeus Seminar: \"Machine Learning for Spectroscopy\"](https://ml4spec25.sciencesconf.org/?lang=en), Brussels (BE): *Responsible for shaping the scientific program, including topic selection, invited speaker coordination, and session chairing.*\n- 2016-2021, **Course representative**, MatNano Engineering, Politecnico di Milano: *represented MatNano students to institute leadership, led monthly feedback meetings.*\n- 2018-03/04, **“Public Speaking” course**, People@DEIB\n\n## Technical Expertise\n- **Python**: data analysis (DuckDB, pandas, NumPy, scikit-learn, marimo), active learning, uncertainty-aware and deep learning for chemistry/materials science (PyTorch, Lightning, JAX, ASE), high-throughput workflows (Pydantic).\n- **Atomistic simulations**: AMS (PLAMS, ParAMS and ADF), ORCA.\n- **Tooling**: Git, GitHub, SVN, Bash, vibe coding (Claude, Codex)","x":240,"y":-34,"width":520,"height":1072},
